        "id": "lem-ip-separable-hilbert-borel-laws-determined-by-orthonormal-coordinates",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "title": "Borel laws on a separable Hilbert space are determined by basis coordinates",
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $H$ be a real Hilbert space with a finite or countable complete orthonormal basis $(e_j)_{j\\in J}$. For each finite $F\\subseteq J$, define the coordinate map $\\pi_F:H\\to\\mathbb R^F$ by $\\pi_F(x)=(\\langle x,e_j\\rangle)_{j\\in F}$. If $\\nu$ and $\\nu'$ are Borel probability measures on $H$ and $\\nu(\\pi_F^{-1}(B))=\\nu'(\\pi_F^{-1}(B))$ for every finite $F\\subseteq J$ and every Borel $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R^F$, then $\\nu=\\nu'$.",
