        "title": "pCN stationary mean acceptance tends to one at small scale",
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $H$ be a separable real Hilbert space and let $\\mu_0$ be a centered Borel Gaussian probability measure on $H$. Let $\\Phi:H\\to[0,\\infty)$ be finite-valued and Borel measurable. Suppose that there are constants $p,K>0$ such that $$0\\le\\Phi(u)\\le K(1+\\|u\\|^p)\\qquad(u\\in H),$$ and for every $R>0$ there is a finite $L_R$ such that $$|\\Phi(u)-\\Phi(v)|\\le L_R\\|u-v\\|\\quad\\text{whenever }\\max\\{\\|u\\|,\\|v\\|\\}<R.$$ Set $Z=\\int_H e^{-\\Phi(u)}\\,\\mu_0(du)$ and $\\mu(du)=Z^{-1}e^{-\\Phi(u)}\\mu_0(du)$. For $\\beta\\in[0,1]$, let $U\\sim\\mu$ and $\\xi\\sim\\mu_0$ be independent, put $V_\\beta=\\sqrt{1-\\beta^2}U+\\beta\\xi$, and define $$\\alpha_\\beta=\\min\\{1,\\exp(\\Phi(U)-\\Phi(V_\\beta))\\}.$$ Then $0<Z<\\infty$, $\\mu$ is a probability measure, and the stationary mean acceptance satisfies $$\\lim_{\\beta\\downarrow0}\\mathbb E[\\alpha_\\beta]=1.$$",
